WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our next guest is nominated
for four Grammy Awards,

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
including Best New Artist,
Best Rock Performance,

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:06.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
Best Rock Song, and
Best Alternative Music Album

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:08.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
for "Punisher,"
which is available now.

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:11.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome back to the sho
Phoebe Bridgers.

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:12.879 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Hi, Phoebe. How are you?

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm great. How are you?
-I'm great.

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:16.716
So this is your third time
technically on the show.

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's the first time
we're chatting.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:21.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were in studio
with Boygenius in 2018.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:24.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then you did a beautiful
film performance

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.493 line:92%
for us during the pandemic

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:29.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it different as an artist
being on a talk show,

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:31.131 size:78% position:39%
one, where you get to
film it ahead of time

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:34.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the other
where you get to be in studio?

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.436 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Um, yeah, I --

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:39.472
I'm honestly going to be
so spoiled after all this

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:41.708 line:92%
because I love the control

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:45.078
I actually -- When I was o
your show with Boygenius,

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:47.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
I yodeled really loud
on accident.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
you can't go back and fix it

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.317 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was a nightmare.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:55.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I like being able to listen
to mixes and make changes.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:56.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is an accidental yodel
something

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:59.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
that happens to you often
or was it just in the moment

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:03.863
-Yeah, I have the accidental
yodel when I hit high note

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:06.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then also an accidenta
Eddie Vedder

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:10.170
where if I hit a really loud
note sometimes I have like..

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.005 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Growls ]

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:13.239 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's pretty rad.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.809 size:81% position:41%
-I will let you know
that I did not notice.

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:18.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
I only thought it was
a wonderful performance.

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:20.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm wondering how weird it is.
You have this album,

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:22.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it receives
all of this praise

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:24.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
and these multiple
Grammy nominations,

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
and yet most of it
is happening at home for you

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:30.356
Has it been an even more surreal
year than it is for most peopl

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you would
have been so out and about

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:36.496
I would imagine,
on the back of this great album?

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:38.198 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yes, it's so weird.

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:39.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hate that, like,
the only connection

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:44.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have to my friends
and the universe is online

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.272 line:92%
Yeah, it feels super weird

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:51.344 size:81% position:41%
Grocery store is where
I hang out. That's it.

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:53.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Another thing that seems --
I don't know --

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Fortuitous" seems
like the wrong word,

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:58.017
but, you know, again, this i
an album that was written,

00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:00.787 size:88% position:44%
recorded ahead of time,
but a lot of the issues,

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:03.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, grief,
family relationships,

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:08.661
the world ending, are very muc
at the forefront of this album

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:11.364
How has that been to know
that you sort of wrote

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:15.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
the perfect album
for a very hard time?

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:18.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I feel like
I'm always having a hard time.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:21.407 line:92%
So, I'm terrified of everything,

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
always think the world
is going to end.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:25.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I think maybe
even if I released

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:26.679 line:92%
my first record around now

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:28.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
people would have thought
it was about COVID,

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:31.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, weirdly,
I think, looking back,

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:33.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
I will remember
the record more from

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I released it
than when I wrote it.

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:40.093 size:88% position:44%
It actually kind of does
remind me of isolation,

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:44.497
I think, 'cause I played
the songs so much in my bedroom.

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:47.433
-I've heard tell that your
neighbors are maybe not thrilled

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:52.472
with living next to a musician
who plays songs in her bedroom

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:54.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are they --
Have they changed their tune

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:57.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
at all based
on the success of the album?

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:59.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have one cool neighbor,
Michael,

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:05.451
who says "what's up?" to me an
knows that I have a real job

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:08.888 size:88% position:44%
but there's one neighbor
that tells me to shut up

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:12.592
and then my next next-door
neighbor plays slap bass,

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:17.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I feel like I'm suffering
from his slap bass.

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:20.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, my acoustic guitar
whispering

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:23.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
after a whole day of slap bass
is just too much.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
You're the tipping point.

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:27.807 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Again, I do think
it's really important

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:32.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
to look at silver linings
over the course
of this last year,

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:36.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I will say I thought
it was really awesome and cool

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:38.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
to see you
on the cover of "Variety."

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:41.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know if you had told m
March 11th last year

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:43.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you were going to be
on the cover of "Variety" --

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:46.092
I would've been like, "Wow. What
kind of year is it going to be?"

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:51.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
So -- But somebody
got edited out of this photo

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:54.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God. I know.
She really did.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.569 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:59.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you -- you brought her
to the photo shoot,

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:02.075 size:78% position:39%
and they took a bunch
with the dog, yes?

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:04.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And then they just iced her

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:07.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
I think there's, like, a video

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
of us doing the photo shoo
that she's in it,

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:11.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
but she's super photogenic
so I don't understand.

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:13.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's just sleeping on my la
right now.

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:16.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it must be, like,
a weird Zoom filter right no

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:17.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
because she looks
a little weird,

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:19.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
but obviously
she's an incredibly --

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:23.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
We can all tell she's
an incredibly beautiful dog.

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:25.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey, one thing
that's really cool --

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:27.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would love to finish
with this -- is you

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.769 line:92%
in the Best Rock category.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:31.337 size:88% position:44% line:92%
It's all female artists.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.172 line:92%
That's never happened before

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:35.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's such a neat thing
to be a part of.

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:37.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you feel a connection
to the nominees?

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know people always say,
"Oh, it's so great

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:41.114 size:81% position:41%
to be nominated with
this group of people,"

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:45.285
but maybe this year that's
even more true than normal

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:46.219 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Definitely, yeah.

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:49.489
I'm such a huge fan of everybody
who put out records,

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:52.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
especially in, like,
the alternative categories

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:55.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just feel like they're peopl
I would have been --

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:59.432
We call it "tour bidding" when
you're, like, on a festival tour

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:01.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you see the same peopl
every day

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.970
because everybody put out
a record at the same time.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:06.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I feel like there are peopl
that I probably

00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:07.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
would have gotten
pretty close with

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:10.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we all released musi
last year,

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:15.915
but being ripped away from that,
it's cool to have somethin

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:20.119
so awesome as the Grammys
bring us kind of closer.

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:23.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Also you released a cover
of a John Prine song,

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:26.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Summer's End,"
and one of the days

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:28.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I feel COVID
most became real to me,

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:31.130
because I was such a fan of his,
was when he passed away

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:34.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
in sort of the early part
of last spring.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.169 line:92%
And I'm assuming he was someon

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:40.440
that you're a fan of
for you to do a cover like that.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that was
the worst day ever.

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:43.409 size:88% position:44% line:92%
It was just, you know --

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:45.945
He'd been struggling
with his health for a long time,

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:48.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he pulled through
and completely relearned

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:50.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
how to sing,
and I saw him in Oslo.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:51.684 size:75% position:38% line:92%
It was the weirdest.

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:56.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
I landed the first day of tour
walked out of the airport,

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:58.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
and saw this huge sign
that was like,

00:05:58.358 --> 00:06:00.126 size:78% position:39% line:92%
"John Prine Tonight."

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:04.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he represents
kind of the pinnacle

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:07.600 line:92%
of, like, American music to me

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:11.204 size:81% position:41%
So I saw him at this,
like, theater in Oslo,

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:13.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
and people
clapping very politely,

00:06:13.506 --> 00:06:17.176
and he talked about American
politics and was so charming

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:18.311 line:92%
And I've seen him a bunch,

00:06:18.311 --> 00:06:20.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, yeah,
that was a very depressing day

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:23.216 size:84% position:42%
and definitely one of
the reasons I chose it.

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:26.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was nominated
for Best New Artist in 1972,

00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:28.054 size:78% position:39% line:92%
which is pretty cool.

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:30.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that is a very nice way
to close this.

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:33.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks for doing that.
Thanks for the album.
And thanks for being here.

00:06:33.126 --> 00:06:34.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just a delight
to see you, Phoebe.

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:37.730
-Yeah, thanks so much, man
-"Punisher" is available now

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:41.134 size:84% position:42%
We will be right back
with more "Late Night."

